# Copy to .env.local for local development; replace placeholders before use.
# Server-only. Never expose these in browser code or commit actual credentials.
# Local PostgreSQL development with a dedicated non-owner login.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://rimdan_app:REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:55432/rimdan_dev
APP_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:3000
APP_ENV=development
PORT=3000
# Migration owner: operator process only, never Vercel runtime.
# Prefer supplying this only to the manual migration/bootstrap process.
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_OWNER_PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:55432/rimdan_dev
# Bootstrap is manual, requires migration 008, and refuses non-empty accounts.
# BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_TEST_EMAIL
# BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_TEST_PASSWORD
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:REPLACE_WITH_DISPOSABLE_TEST_PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:55432/postgres
# Supabase manual setup: see WINDOWS_SETUP.md. Disable the unused Data API first.
# Shared TRANSACTION pooler runtime URL (copy actual host from Dashboard > Connect):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://rimdan_app.PROJECT_REF:URL_ENCODED_PASSWORD@ACTUAL_POOLER_HOST:6543/postgres?sslmode=verify-full
# Direct custom-role username is rimdan_app; shared pooler is rimdan_app.PROJECT_REF.
# Production APP_ORIGIN must be the exact HTTPS origin; APP_ENV=production.
# Verify TLS certificates AND hostnames using the downloaded provider root CA:
# DATABASE_SSL_CA="-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
# REPLACE_WITH_PROVIDER_CA_PEM
# -----END CERTIFICATE-----"
# Or append &sslrootcert=C%3A%2Fsecure%2Fsupabase-ca.crt to the URL on Windows.
# CA files must exist on that machine; for Vercel use DATABASE_SSL_CA PEM instead.
# Never use sslmode=require/no-verify, ssl=false, NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0,
# URL host/user overrides, or API keys as PostgreSQL database passwords.
# Operator-only direct URL (never put this in Vercel or normal runtime settings):
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:URL_ENCODED_OWNER_PASSWORD@db.PROJECT_REF.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=verify-full
# IPv4 alternative: shared SESSION pooler, postgres.PROJECT_REF, port 5432.
# Run node scripts/migrate.js --approve-production, then verify-isolation.js
# --approve-production --require-api-roles. Remove operator variables afterward.
# RIMDAN_MODE is intentionally omitted: normal builds use authenticated server mode.

# Phase-one readiness: node --env-file=.env.local scripts/check-runtime.js
# uses DATABASE_URL (rimdan_app), never MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL.
# /api/v1/config validates configuration, not network readiness.
# /api/v1/ready requires an Administrator session and returns only {"ready":true}.
# Existing deployments already have migrations 001-008 and an Administrator:
# do not bootstrap again for this application-only update.
